246
00:16:35,536 --> 00:16:37,913
It's a little spooky, isn't it?

247
00:16:46,673 --> 00:16:48,298
Oh, l'm not carrying that.

248
00:16:50,551 --> 00:16:52,427
It could go off.

249
00:16:54,972 --> 00:16:56,139
I'll man the flashlight.

250
00:16:58,017 --> 00:16:59,059
You do that.

251
00:17:12,949 --> 00:17:15,033
[EMF METER HUMMlNG]

252
00:17:27,422 --> 00:17:30,257
EMF's not gonna work with me around,
is it?

253
00:17:30,466 --> 00:17:31,758
[EXHALES]

254
00:17:32,301 --> 00:17:33,552
You don't say.

255
00:17:36,055 --> 00:17:37,723
Come on.

256
00:17:39,976 --> 00:17:41,351
[GASPS]

257
00:17:46,774 --> 00:17:50,026
"To Frank, Love Jessie."

258
00:17:50,278 --> 00:17:52,487
Frank O'Brian's ring.

259
00:17:52,655 --> 00:17:54,948
What the hell was Frank doing here?

260
00:17:55,450 --> 00:17:56,616
No idea.

261
00:18:08,087 --> 00:18:10,172
[THUMPlNG]

262
00:18:23,770 --> 00:18:24,811
[MOUTHS]
On three.

263
00:18:25,938 --> 00:18:28,940
One, two, three.

264
00:18:29,609 --> 00:18:33,361
[SCREAMlNG]

265
00:18:33,696 --> 00:18:34,821
[PANTlNG]

266
00:18:37,658 --> 00:18:39,826
That was scary.

267
00:18:43,956 --> 00:18:45,248
What?

268
00:19:10,691 --> 00:19:12,859
SAM:
"Luther Garland."

269
00:19:15,738 --> 00:19:16,780
Hey, this is....

270
00:19:18,950 --> 00:19:21,076
This is Frank's wife.

271
00:19:21,244 --> 00:19:23,161
The plot thickens.

272
00:19:23,329 --> 00:19:25,747
Yeah, but into what?

273
00:19:27,083 --> 00:19:29,084
[MACHlNES THUDDING]

274
00:19:30,086 --> 00:19:31,586
[GASPS]

275
00:19:57,113 --> 00:19:58,780
SAM:
Hey.

276
00:20:17,133 --> 00:20:18,633
[SAM PANTS]

277
00:20:19,135 --> 00:20:21,428
I guess we got the right place.

278
00:20:29,979 --> 00:20:33,273
-This is the Garland file.
-Thanks. Ahem.

279
00:20:41,240 --> 00:20:43,575
Is he drunk?

280
00:20:48,581 --> 00:20:49,998
No.

281
00:20:50,207 --> 00:20:53,126
Deputy, according to this,
Luther Garland's cause of death...

282
00:20:53,294 --> 00:20:56,004
...was physical trauma.
Now, what does that mean?

283
00:20:56,672 --> 00:21:00,342
Guy died 20 years ago.
Before my time. Sorry.

284
00:21:00,509 --> 00:21:02,802
Then can we talk to the sheriff?

285
00:21:03,179 --> 00:21:05,347
-Um.... He's out sick today.
-Well, if you see him...

286
00:21:05,514 --> 00:21:08,350
...will you have him call us?
We're staying at the Bluebird.

287
00:21:08,517 --> 00:21:10,268
Mind if I take this?

288
00:21:14,440 --> 00:21:16,191
Know what?

289
00:21:17,944 --> 00:21:19,027
You're awesome.

290
00:21:19,362 --> 00:21:22,364
Heh. Ha.

291
00:21:22,865 --> 00:21:24,532
Thanks.

292
00:21:25,368 --> 00:21:27,035
You too, l guess.

293
00:21:27,244 --> 00:21:28,328
[CHUCKLES]

294
00:21:28,496 --> 00:21:30,455
[CLEARS THROAT]

295
00:21:30,873 --> 00:21:31,957
[DOOR OPENS]

296
00:21:32,124 --> 00:21:33,333
AL [OVER SPEAKER]:
Who was that?

297
00:21:33,501 --> 00:21:37,003
-lt-- Those FBl guys.
-What did they want?

298
00:21:37,880 --> 00:21:40,799
A file. Luther Garland's.

299
00:21:43,636 --> 00:21:45,303
Sheriff?

300
00:21:50,685 --> 00:21:52,727
MAN [lN VOICEOVER]:
They know.

301
00:21:55,398 --> 00:21:57,649
They know.

302
00:21:59,860 --> 00:22:01,403
They know what you did.

303
00:22:02,530 --> 00:22:04,823
And now they're gonna make you pay.

304
00:22:06,492 --> 00:22:08,410
[SINISTER CHUCKLING]

305
00:22:10,329 --> 00:22:11,746
[DEAN GASPS]

306
00:22:14,583 --> 00:22:17,752
This isn't gonna work. These badges
are fake. What if we get busted?

307
00:22:17,920 --> 00:22:18,920
We could go to jail.

308
00:22:19,088 --> 00:22:21,923
Dean, shh, calm down.
Deep breath, okay?

309
00:22:22,091 --> 00:22:25,093
[BOTH BREATHE DEEPLY]

310
00:22:25,261 --> 00:22:27,220
There. You feel better?

311
00:22:27,763 --> 00:22:29,764
Just come on.

312
00:22:30,599 --> 00:22:32,434
Don't scratch.

313
00:22:39,608 --> 00:22:40,942
[SAM CLEARS THROAT]

314
00:22:41,110 --> 00:22:42,193
SAM:
Mr. Garland?

315
00:22:42,361 --> 00:22:44,195
Hi.

316
00:22:44,363 --> 00:22:46,781
I'm Agent Tyler,
this is Agent Perry, FBl.

317
00:22:46,949 --> 00:22:50,618
We'd like to ask you a few questions
about your brother, Luther.

318
00:22:51,746 --> 00:22:54,914
-Let me see some lD.
SAM: Certainly.

319
00:22:56,250 --> 00:22:57,625
[CLEARS THROAT]

320
00:23:06,719 --> 00:23:07,886
Those are real.

321
00:23:09,722 --> 00:23:11,473
-Obviously.
-Ahem.

322
00:23:12,933 --> 00:23:16,352
I mean, who would pretend to be
an FBl agent, huh? That's just nutty.

323
00:23:16,562 --> 00:23:17,771
[SAM KlCKS DEAN]

324
00:23:23,486 --> 00:23:24,736
GARLAND:
What do you want to know?

325
00:23:25,821 --> 00:23:31,493
Uh-- Well, according to this, your
brother, Luther, died of physical trauma.

326
00:23:31,660 --> 00:23:32,786
[SCOFFS]

327
00:23:32,953 --> 00:23:35,330
-You don't agree?
-No, I don't.

328
00:23:35,498 --> 00:23:37,290
Well, then what would you call it?

329
00:23:37,792 --> 00:23:40,085
Don't matter what an old man thinks.

330
00:23:41,504 --> 00:23:44,756
Mr. Garland, we're just trying
to get the truth on your brother.

331
00:23:45,674 --> 00:23:47,008
Please.

332
00:23:52,973 --> 00:23:55,642
Everybody was scared of Luther.

333
00:23:56,268 --> 00:23:57,894
They called him a monster.

334
00:23:59,396 --> 00:24:02,524
He was too big, too mean-looking.

335
00:24:04,110 --> 00:24:06,694
Just too different.

336
00:24:11,909 --> 00:24:14,702
Didn't matter that he was
the kindest man l ever knew.

337
00:24:14,870 --> 00:24:18,331
Didn't matter he'd never hurt no one.

338
00:24:23,212 --> 00:24:27,173
A lot of people failed Luther,
I was one of them.

339
00:24:27,800 --> 00:24:32,053
I was a widower
with three young ones and...

340
00:24:32,221 --> 00:24:36,015
...l told myself
there was nothing l could do.

341
00:24:37,977 --> 00:24:39,144
Mr. Garland.

342
00:24:41,230 --> 00:24:43,648
Do you recognize this woman?

343
00:24:45,568 --> 00:24:48,153
That's Jessie O'Brian.

344
00:24:49,530 --> 00:24:51,364
Her man, Frank, killed Luther.

345
00:24:53,909 --> 00:24:56,578
-How do you know that?
-Everybody knows.

346
00:24:56,745 --> 00:24:58,580
They just don't talk about it.

347
00:24:59,248 --> 00:25:02,750
Jessie was a receptionist at the mill.

348
00:25:04,587 --> 00:25:10,091
She was always real nice to Luther,
and he had a crush on her.

349
00:25:10,259 --> 00:25:12,594
But Frank didn't like it.

350
00:25:12,761 --> 00:25:14,345
Then when Jessie went missing...

351
00:25:14,847 --> 00:25:17,724
...Frank was sure that
Luther had done something to her.

352
00:25:19,727 --> 00:25:24,063
Turns out the old gal killed herself,
but Frank didn't know that.

353
00:25:36,952 --> 00:25:38,077
[COCKS GUN]

354
00:25:49,757 --> 00:25:51,257
[ENGINE STARTS]

355
00:25:51,592 --> 00:25:53,635
[TlRES SQUEALING]

356
00:25:54,553 --> 00:25:58,056
They found Luther
with a chain wrapped around his neck.

357
00:25:58,224 --> 00:26:01,434
He was dragged up and down
the stretch outside that plant...

358
00:26:01,602 --> 00:26:03,394
...till he was past dead.

359
00:26:03,562 --> 00:26:05,396
And O'Brian was never arrested?

360
00:26:05,981 --> 00:26:08,149
I screamed to every cop in town.

361
00:26:08,817 --> 00:26:10,902
They wouldn't look into Frank.

362
00:26:11,070 --> 00:26:13,321
He was a pillar of the community.

363
00:26:13,530 --> 00:26:15,490
My brother was just the town freak.

364
00:26:15,658 --> 00:26:17,408
You must have hated Frank O'Brian.

365
00:26:17,576 --> 00:26:22,330
I did for a long time,
but, heh, life's too short for hate, son.

366
00:26:22,915 --> 00:26:28,294
Frank wasn't thinking straight.
His wife had vanished, he was terrified.

367
00:26:28,462 --> 00:26:31,589
A damn shame he had to
put Luther through the same...

368
00:26:32,299 --> 00:26:34,342
...but that's fear.

369
00:26:34,843 --> 00:26:37,512
It spreads and spreads.

370
00:26:42,184 --> 00:26:44,519
Now I know what these are: road rash.

371
00:26:44,687 --> 00:26:47,188
And l'm guessing Luther
swallowed some wood chips...

372
00:26:47,356 --> 00:26:49,857
...when he was
being dragged down that road.

373
00:26:50,025 --> 00:26:53,611
It makes sense. You're experiencing
his death in slow motion.

374
00:26:53,779 --> 00:26:58,366
Yeah, well, not slow enough. l say
we burn some bones and get me healthy.

375
00:26:59,034 --> 00:27:00,535
Dean, it won't be that easy.

376
00:27:00,703 --> 00:27:03,830
No, no, it'll be that easy.
Why won't it be that easy?

377
00:27:03,998 --> 00:27:07,375
Luther was road-hauled.
His body was ripped to pieces.

378
00:27:07,543 --> 00:27:10,878
He was probably
scattered all over that road.

379
00:27:11,088 --> 00:27:14,299
There's no way
we're gonna find all the remains.

380
00:27:15,384 --> 00:27:16,467
You're kidding me.

381
00:27:16,635 --> 00:27:19,387
Look, we'll just have to
figure something else out.

382
00:27:20,723 --> 00:27:22,390
You know what? Screw this.

383
00:27:22,558 --> 00:27:25,310
-Whoa, whoa, Dean, come on--
-No, I mean, come on, Sam.

384
00:27:26,603 --> 00:27:28,062
What are we doing?

385
00:27:28,230 --> 00:27:31,357
-We're hunting a ghost.
-A Ghost, exactly. Who does that?

386
00:27:31,900 --> 00:27:34,569
-Us.
-Us. Right.

387
00:27:34,737 --> 00:27:37,572
And that, Sam,
that is exactly why our lives suck.

388
00:27:37,740 --> 00:27:40,908
I mean, come on, we hunt monsters.
What the hell?

389
00:27:41,410 --> 00:27:45,079
I mean, normal people, they see a
monster, and they run. But not us, no.

390
00:27:45,247 --> 00:27:48,666
We search out things
that want to kill us. Huh? Huh?

391
00:27:48,834 --> 00:27:50,668
Or eat us.

392
00:27:50,836 --> 00:27:52,920
You know who does that?
Crazy people.

393
00:27:53,088 --> 00:27:55,757
We are insane.

394
00:27:55,924 --> 00:27:59,260
And then there's the bad diner food,
and then skeevy motel rooms...

395
00:27:59,428 --> 00:28:02,055
...and the truck-stop waitress
with the bizarre rash--

396
00:28:02,222 --> 00:28:05,266
I mean, who wants this life, Sam, huh?
Seriously?

397
00:28:05,434 --> 00:28:10,063
Do you actually like being stuck in a car
with me 8 hours a day, every single day?

398
00:28:10,230 --> 00:28:13,691
I don't think so. l drive too fast,
I listen to the same five albums...

399
00:28:13,859 --> 00:28:17,111
...over and over again, and l sing along.
I'm annoying, l know that.

400
00:28:17,279 --> 00:28:19,238
And you, you're gassy.

401
00:28:20,115 --> 00:28:23,576
You eat half a burrito and you get toxic.
I mean-- You know what?

402
00:28:23,744 --> 00:28:26,454
-You can forget it.
-Oh. Dean, where are you going?

403
00:28:26,622 --> 00:28:29,290
Stay away from me, Sam, okay?
Because I am done with it.

404
00:28:29,458 --> 00:28:32,960
I'm done with the monsters and the
hellhounds, and the ghost sickness...

405
00:28:33,170 --> 00:28:34,796
...and the damn Apocalypse.

406
00:28:35,422 --> 00:28:37,965
I'm out. l'm done. l quit.

407
00:28:38,175 --> 00:28:39,801
[KEYS JlNGLE]

408
00:28:39,968 --> 00:28:41,469
[GROANS]

409
00:28:46,683 --> 00:28:48,768
[BREATHlNG HEAVlLY]

410
00:28:49,770 --> 00:28:51,813
[FLAPPING]

411
00:28:51,980 --> 00:28:54,065
[DOG GROWLS]

412
00:29:07,788 --> 00:29:09,956
I looked everywhere for you, Dean.

413
00:29:10,124 --> 00:29:12,291
How the hell did you get here?

414
00:29:12,835 --> 00:29:14,001
Ran.

415
00:29:16,839 --> 00:29:18,297
[SIGHS]

416
00:29:23,804 --> 00:29:25,763
What do we do now?

417
00:29:26,098 --> 00:29:29,016
I mean, l got less than
four hours on the clock.

418
00:29:29,351 --> 00:29:30,810
[SIGHS]

419
00:29:31,145 --> 00:29:32,437
I'm gonna die, Sammy.

420
00:29:33,355 --> 00:29:35,148
Yeah, you are.

421
00:29:36,024 --> 00:29:37,316
You're going back.

422
00:29:38,444 --> 00:29:42,029
-Back?
-Downstairs, Dean. Hell.

423
00:29:43,449 --> 00:29:45,616
It's about damn time too.

424
00:29:45,784 --> 00:29:49,537
Truth is,
you've been a real pain in my ass.

425
00:29:53,542 --> 00:29:56,878
No. You get out of my brother,
you evil son of a bitch!

426
00:29:57,045 --> 00:29:59,714
No one's possessing me, Dean.

427
00:29:59,882 --> 00:30:04,635
This is what l'm going to become.
This is what l want to become.

428
00:30:04,803 --> 00:30:06,804
And there's nothing
you can do about it.

429
00:30:08,307 --> 00:30:09,724
[GRUNTlNG]

430
00:30:13,395 --> 00:30:16,814
Hey, hey, hey, Dean.
Hey, Dean. Dean. Dean.

431
00:30:16,982 --> 00:30:18,149
[PANTlNG]

432
00:30:28,827 --> 00:30:30,203
[CAR APPROACHlNG]

433
00:30:34,041 --> 00:30:36,709
-Howdy, Sam.
-Hey, Bobby.

434
00:30:36,877 --> 00:30:39,170
Thanks for coming up so quick.

435
00:30:40,214 --> 00:30:41,756
Where's Dean?

436
00:30:41,924 --> 00:30:44,342
Uh.... Heh.

437
00:30:44,510 --> 00:30:45,551
Home, sick.

438
00:30:45,719 --> 00:30:49,931
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC
OVER TV PLAYING]

439
00:30:54,394 --> 00:30:55,895
Oh, this isn't helping.

440
00:30:56,063 --> 00:30:58,231
So have his hallucinations started yet?

441
00:30:58,398 --> 00:31:00,942
-Yeah, a few hours ago.
-How are we doing on time?

442
00:31:01,151 --> 00:31:04,362
We saw the coroner
about 8 a.m. Monday morning.

443
00:31:04,863 --> 00:31:07,114
So just under two hours.

444
00:31:07,282 --> 00:31:08,950
What about you? You find anything?

445
00:31:09,117 --> 00:31:13,955
This encyclopedia of spirits
dates to the Edo period.

446
00:31:15,082 --> 00:31:16,707
You can read Japanese?

447
00:31:16,959 --> 00:31:19,877
[SPEAKS IN JAPANESE]

448
00:31:20,087 --> 00:31:22,296
I guess so. Showoff.

449
00:31:22,464 --> 00:31:26,050
BOBBY: Anyway, this book lists
a kind of ghost that could be our guy.

450
00:31:26,218 --> 00:31:29,637
It infects people with fear.
It's called a Buru Buru.

451
00:31:29,805 --> 00:31:32,974
-Does it say how to kill it?
-Same as usual, burn the remains.

452
00:31:33,141 --> 00:31:34,809
Wonderful.

453
00:31:34,977 --> 00:31:37,270
Is there a plan B?

454
00:31:37,437 --> 00:31:42,817
Well, the Buru Buru is born of fear.
Hell, it is fear.

455
00:31:42,985 --> 00:31:45,486
And the lore says
you can kill it with fear.

456
00:31:45,988 --> 00:31:49,073
-So we have to scare a ghost to death?
-Pretty much.

457
00:31:51,326 --> 00:31:53,202
How the hell are we gonna do that?

458
00:31:53,704 --> 00:31:55,788
[CELL PHONE PLAYS RlNGTONE]

459
00:31:59,960 --> 00:32:01,085
-Hey.
SAM [OVER PHONE]: Hey.

460
00:32:01,253 --> 00:32:05,464
So just ride out the trip, okay?
You're gonna be fine. We got a plan.

461
00:32:05,966 --> 00:32:07,008
Ugh.

462
00:32:07,175 --> 00:32:09,677
-What is it?
-Just a good plan, all right?

463
00:32:09,845 --> 00:32:11,345
Now, hang in there.

464
00:32:15,267 --> 00:32:18,227
-This is a terrible plan.
-Yeah, tell me about it.

465
00:32:18,770 --> 00:32:21,522
I know l said scare the ghost
to death, but this?

466
00:32:22,024 --> 00:32:24,317
Hey, you got a better idea,
I'm listening.

467
00:32:56,475 --> 00:32:58,559
[ANlMALS HOWLlNG lN DlSTANCE]

468
00:33:01,480 --> 00:33:03,272
[DOGS SNARLlNG, BARKING]

469
00:33:03,899 --> 00:33:05,358
[POUNDING ON DOOR]

470
00:33:12,366 --> 00:33:13,532
[MAN GRUNTS]

471
00:33:17,204 --> 00:33:18,829
Sheriff.

472
00:33:20,082 --> 00:33:21,415
What are you doing?

473
00:33:21,917 --> 00:33:24,335
Why are you looking into
Luther Garland's death?

474
00:33:25,587 --> 00:33:28,881
Hey. Hey, you're sick.
You're sick, you're sick, all right?

475
00:33:29,049 --> 00:33:31,592
Just like me, okay? You gotta relax.

476
00:33:31,802 --> 00:33:33,052
[GRUNTS]

477
00:33:33,220 --> 00:33:35,846
Frank O'Brian was my friend.

478
00:33:36,014 --> 00:33:40,434
So he made a mistake.
So l didn't bust him. So what?

479
00:33:41,395 --> 00:33:44,021
And you're gonna
bring me down over that?

480
00:33:44,189 --> 00:33:46,357
No, sir.

481
00:33:46,525 --> 00:33:48,025
[GUN CLATTERS]

482
00:33:48,360 --> 00:33:50,444
[GRUNTlNG]

483
00:34:10,632 --> 00:34:12,758
[PANTlNG]

484
00:34:17,472 --> 00:34:19,390
[IN VOlCEOVER]
They know what you did.

485
00:34:19,558 --> 00:34:20,933
Get away from me.

486
00:34:21,101 --> 00:34:23,060
-Al, you gotta calm down.
-Get back!

487
00:34:24,354 --> 00:34:26,105
[GASPlNG]

488
00:34:44,875 --> 00:34:46,584
BOBBY [OVER WALKIE-TALKlE]:
Any luck?

489
00:34:49,171 --> 00:34:53,674
I don't know what's wrong, Bobby.
Last time he came right at us.

490
00:34:53,842 --> 00:34:56,177
It's almost like he's....

491
00:34:58,013 --> 00:34:59,680
Like he's scared.

492
00:34:59,890 --> 00:35:01,307
[WALKlE-TALKIE SQUAWKS]

493
00:35:08,023 --> 00:35:09,106
So now what?

494
00:35:10,108 --> 00:35:11,609
I guess I gotta make him angry.

495
00:35:16,698 --> 00:35:18,699
Hey, Luther.

496
00:35:25,707 --> 00:35:28,334
Come on, Luther.
